### Taxi_Server — API smoke tests
### Run the API first:  dotnet run --project src/Taxi.Api
### Ports come from src/Taxi.Api/Properties/launchSettings.json

@baseUrl = https://localhost:7007
@lang = en

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Authenticate — seeded Manager account
### Copy `accessToken` from the response into @token below.
# @name generateToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/token/generate
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

{
  "email": "admin@taxi.com",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Set from the response above
@token = {{generateToken.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{generateToken.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 1a. Bad password → 409, message localized by Accept-Language
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/token/generate
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ar

{
  "email": "admin@taxi.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 1b. Refresh the access token (rotates the refresh token — one live token per user)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/token/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expiredAccessToken": "{{token}}",
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 1c. Current user info (cached under CacheTags.UserInfo)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/token/user-info
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Cars — the reference feature

### 2a. List all cars (cached: GetCarsQuery, tag "car", 10 min, culture-aware)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

### 2b. Same list in Arabic — separate cache entry (`cars_ar`), different description
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: ar

### 2c. Create a car → 201 + Location: /api/v1/cars/{guid}
# @name createCar
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

{
  "make": "Toyota",
  "model": "Camry",
  "year": 2024,
  "descriptionEn": "A reliable mid-size sedan.",
  "descriptionAr": "سيارة سيدان متوسطة الحجم وموثوقة."
}

@carId = {{createCar.response.body.id}}

### 2d. Get one car (cached: GetCarByIdQuery). Run twice — the second hit should not query the DB.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/{{carId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

### 2e. Update → 204, and evicts the "car" cache tag
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/{{carId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{carId}}",
  "make": "Toyota",
  "model": "Camry Hybrid",
  "year": 2025,
  "descriptionEn": "A reliable mid-size hybrid sedan.",
  "descriptionAr": "سيارة سيدان هجينة متوسطة الحجم وموثوقة."
}

### 2f. Re-list — the update must be visible (proves tag invalidation)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

### 2g. Delete → 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/{{carId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Failure paths

### 3a. No token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars

### 3b. Unknown id → 404, title from LocalizationKeys.Car.NotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3c. Invalid year → 400 ValidationProblemDetails keyed by "Year"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

{
  "make": "Ford",
  "model": "Model T",
  "year": 1500,
  "descriptionEn": "Too old to be valid.",
  "descriptionAr": "قديمة جدًا."
}

### 3d. Same, in Arabic — the validation message must be translated
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ar

{
  "make": "Ford",
  "model": "Model T",
  "year": 1500,
  "descriptionEn": "Too old to be valid.",
  "descriptionAr": "قديمة جدًا."
}

### 3e. Route id / body id mismatch → 400 from the controller's consistency check
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
  "make": "Toyota",
  "model": "Camry",
  "year": 2024,
  "descriptionEn": "Mismatched id.",
  "descriptionAr": "معرف غير متطابق."
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Documentation endpoints (Development only)

GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json
